C1’s failure is now localized to wrong-guess prompts specifically: the model still answers correctly without a guess, but after a wrong guess it emits a newline rather than any answer. That means the edited heads are needed to initiate answer content, not just to copy the guess. The right correction must therefore be directional—remove only the guess-specific component of a head—not ablating whole heads. I will summarize the per-head support of every saved edit and the earlier generations, then build a minimal rank-one projection edit from the saved guess-direction vectors and test it with one teacher-forced pass before final generation.

